      "summary": "SFCC-126-TC-09: New Registration on US International Stored on Global Customer List",
      "description": "Story:\n SFCC-126 | \nPriority:\n High | \nLabels:\n @SFCC-126 @account @p0\nComponent:\n My Account — Registration | \nOwner:\n Squad A\n⚠️ BLOCKED: The US International SFCC site ID (ZimmermannUSIntl) is TBC pending Business Manager confirmation (REG-005). This test case cannot be executed until the storefront is reachable in the SIT environment. Test environment URL below is a placeholder — confirm with the integration team before executing.\nNote: US International uses Global-e for checkout (REG-005). Marketing opt-in is pre-checked by default on US storefronts (REG-057).\nObjective:\nVerify registering on the US international storefront (ZimmermannUSIntl) creates an account on the global customer list so the same credentials authenticate on ZimmermannUK without re-registration.\nPreconditions:\nZimmermannUSIntl site ID confirmed in SFCC Business Manager and storefront is reachable in SIT.\nTest email has never been registered in the target SFCC environment.\nSFCC-126 is deployed (global customer list configured).\nTester is not authenticated — fresh browser session.\nreCAPTCHA is set to test-bypass mode (CRM-008).\nTest Steps — Part 1: Register on US international storefront\n#\nAction\nTest Data\nExpected Result\n1\nNavigate to the US international storefront\nhttps://zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/en-ca/ ⚠️ URL TBC\nPage loads at /en-ca/\n2\nDidomi consent banner — click \"Decline tracking\"\n—\nBanner dismisses\n3\nClick \"Account\" in the site header\n—\nNavigates to .../en-ca/login\n4\nClick \"Create Account\" link\n—\nNavigates to .../en-ca/registration\n5\nIn the \"First name\" field\nQA_USIntl\nField populated\n6\nIn the \"Last name\" field\nGlobalTestUSIntl\nField populated\n7\nIn the \"Email\" field\nqa-global-usintl-{timestamp}@zimmermann-test.com\nField populated\n8\nIn the \"Password\" field\nValid password (CRM-006)\nField populated; show/hide toggle present (CRM-016)\n9\nIn the \"Confirm password\" field\nSame as step 8\nNo mismatch error\n10\nNote: marketing opt-in is pre-checked by default on US storefronts (REG-057) — leave as-is\nPre-checked\nCheckbox checked\n11\nClick \"Create Account\" button\n—\nSFCC creates record on global customer list\n12\nVerify redirect to US international account dashboard\n—\nURL: .../en-ca/account; greeting \"Hi QA_USIntl\" (CRM-020)\n13\nClick \"Logout\" in left-hand nav\n—\nSession cleared; no auth cookies remain\nTest Steps — Part 2: Authenticate on UK storefront\n#\nAction\nTest Data\nExpected Result\n14\nNavigate to the UK storefront\nhttps://zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/uk/\nPage loads at /uk/\n15\nDidomi consent banner — click \"Decline tracking\"\n—\nBanner dismisses\n16\nClick \"Account\" in the site header\n—\nNavigates to .../uk/login\n17\nIn the \"Email\" field\nSame email from step 7\nField populated\n18\nIn the \"Password\" field\nSame password from step 8\nField populated\n19\nClick \"Sign In\" button\n—\nSFCC authenticates against global customer list\n20\nWait for navigation to UK account dashboard\n—\nURL: .../uk/account\n21\nVerify personalised welcome message\nExpected first name: QA_USIntl\nGreeting reads \"Hi QA_USIntl\" (CRM-020); no error\nPass Criteria:\n Customer authenticates on UK storefront using US International-registered credentials. Account not scoped to ZimmermannUSIntl.",
